  "body": "For example,\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// Assume we start with `el` already having the `foo` attribute:\r\nel.toggleAttribute('foo', 'bar') // no longer has attribute `foo`\r\nel.toggleAttribute('foo', 'bar') // now has attribute `foo` with value `bar`\r\nel.toggleAttribute('foo', 'bar') // no longer has attribute `foo`\r\nel.toggleAttribute('foo', 'bar') // now has attribute `foo` with value `bar`\r\n```\r\n\r\n- If the attribute exists, remove it. This is similar to calling `removeAttribute('foo')` while the attribute exists.\r\n- If the attribute does not exist, add it, with the given value. This is similar to calling `setAttribute('foo', 'bar')` while the attribute does not exist.\r\n\r\nThe above code would be equivalent to this:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// Assume we start with `el` already having the `foo` attribute:\r\nel.removeAttribute('foo') // no longer has attribute `foo`\r\nel.setAttribute('foo', 'bar') // now has attribute `foo` with value `bar`\r\nel.removeAttribute('foo') // no longer has attribute `foo`\r\nel.setAttribute('foo', 'bar') // now has attribute `foo` with value `bar`\r\n```",
